    "wiredmenu.error_info.delayed_events_cap.2": "If this appears often, the setup is likely relying too heavily on delayed effects and should be simplified.",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.execution_cap.0": "This error occurs when the maximum Wired usage limit is about to be exceeded by a Wired execution.",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.execution_cap.1": "When this happens, the current execution is cancelled so the room never goes over the configured usage budget.",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.execution_cap.2": "If this happens too often, it usually means the setup is too complex for the amount of triggers firing in a short time.",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.executor_overload.0": "This error occurs when the Wired engine is receiving a lot of instructions and the room cannot keep up with the execution time.",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.executor_overload.1": "This can be a sign of server pressure or of a setup that is too expensive to evaluate repeatedly.",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.executor_overload.2": "If the room is also marked as heavy, it is a good sign that the setup should be reduced or optimized.",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.killed.0": "This happens when the room is temporarily halted by the protection layer because the Wired flow looks abusive or unstable.",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.killed.1": "While the room is killed, Wired execution is paused for a cooldown period.",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.killed.2": "This is usually caused by loops, event spam, or repeated limit violations.",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.latest": "Latest occurrence:",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.marked_as_heavy.0": "The room is being considered heavy because its Wired usage stays high across multiple monitor windows.",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.marked_as_heavy.1": "This is not a fatal error by itself, but it means the room is consuming a significant portion of the execution budget.",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.marked_as_heavy.2": "If the room is not intentionally complex, it is worth reviewing the setup before it starts triggering harder limits.",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.motivation": "Motivation:",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.no_targets.0": "A chain fired and one of its effects had nothing to act on, so it did nothing.",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.no_targets.1": "The reason names which source came back empty. \"The triggering item\" is empty when the trigger is not about a furni at all; \"the selector\" is empty when no selector picked anything; \"the picked furni\" is empty when the chosen furni have since been taken up.",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.no_targets.2": "This is not an engine error. It means the setup asked for something that was not there, which until now was the one way a chain could fail in complete silence.",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.occurred_at": "Occurred at:",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.recursion_timeout.0": "Recursive Wired events happen when signals keep re-triggering other stacks in the same room.",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.recursion_timeout.1": "When the recursion depth limit is reached, execution is stopped to prevent runaway loops.",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.recursion_timeout.2": "In most cases this means two or more stacks are indirectly calling each other too many times.",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.title": "Wired Error Information",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.trigger": "Trigger:",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.unreachable.0": "A furni in this room is waiting on something the room has no way of producing, so it will sit there doing nothing.",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.unreachable.1": "A highscore board is the usual case: it only fills when a game ends, and a game can only end through a game timer. Without one in the room the board stays empty forever.",
    "wiredmenu.error_info.unreachable.2": "Nothing has failed. The furni is fine and so is the engine - the room is simply missing the piece that would feed it.",
    "wiredmenu.error_message.7": "Only the owner of this variable can perform this action.",
